description: Never add Cursor/agent attribution to git commits or PRs
alwaysApply: true
---

# No Cursor commit attribution

Never add any of these to commit messages, PR bodies, or git trailers:

- `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`
- `Co-authored-by: Cursor Agent`
- `Made-with: Cursor`
- `--trailer` flags that attribute work to Cursor/agent

When committing, use only the subject/body the user asked for. If the environment injects a Cursor trailer anyway, strip it before finishing (amend only when amend rules allow; otherwise a follow-up commit that only cleans history is wrong — prefer `commit-msg` hook / rewrite).
